		<item>
		<title>Global democracy crisis: How Russia exploits West&#8217;s loss of faith to win its war</title>
		<link>https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/10/12/far-right-parties-on-rise-in-entire-world-as-democracy-wanes-while-moscow-backs-forces-undermining-support-for-ukraine/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Olena Mukhina]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sun, 12 Oct 2025 17:36:08 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Latest news Ukraine]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[democracy]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[democracy crisis]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Europe]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[populism]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Simon Tisdall]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[The Guardian]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[US]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://euromaidanpress.com/?p=366172</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[Across the West and beyond, citizens lose hope in democratic systems, fueling populist movements and political instability.]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><img width="600" height="400" src="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/germans.webp" class="attachment-large size-large wp-post-image" alt="germans" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/germans.webp 600w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/germans-300x200.webp 300w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/germans-380x253.webp 380w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 600px) 100vw, 600px" /></p><div data-type="_mgwidget" data-widget-id="1845881"></div>        
        <script>
            (function(w,q){w[q]=w[q]||[];w[q].push(["_mgc.load"])})(window,"_mgq");
        </script>
    <h3 id="russias-playbook-fueling-europes-far-right-to-cut-aid-for-ukraine" class="ng-star-inserted"><span class="ng-star-inserted">Russia's playbook: Fueling Europe's far-right to cut aid for Ukraine</span></h3>
<p>The world is experiencing an <strong>unprecedented crisis of democracy</strong>. Democratic institutions in <strong>Europe and the US are faltering</strong>, and in developing countries, societies are beginning to question whether building democracy is the right path, writes <strong>Simon Tisdall</strong>, an international affairs commentator, for <strong>The Guardian</strong>.</p>
<div class="pk-content-block pk-block-bg pk-block-bg-light">Russia actively supports and exploits <strong>far-right forces and organizations</strong> to <a target="_blank" href="https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/10/us-far-right-groups-russia-links?" rel="noopener">achieve</a> its geopolitical goals, particularly to secure its victory in the war. These parties <strong>exploit fear, poverty, and the war of attrition</strong>, spreading propaganda. Far-right politicians <a target="_blank" href="https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/10/04/anti%E2%80%91ukrainian-ex%E2%80%91pm-andrej-babiss-party-wins-czech-election-ukraines-arms-lifeline-now-hangs-by-a-thread/" rel="noopener">coming</a> to power <strong><a target="_blank" href="https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/09/13/polish-parliament-adopts-new-law-on-aid-to-ukrainians-after-nawrockis-veto/" rel="noopener">cut</a> aid to Ukraine</strong>, <a target="_blank" href="https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/02/26/romanian-far-right-russia-linked-candidate-questioned-as-police-uncover-weapons-e-900000-in-raids/" rel="noopener">blaming</a> the victim of aggression — Ukraine — for the war that Russia started in 2014. <span style="font-size: revert;">The longer the war continues, the </span><strong>presumably</strong><span style="font-size: revert;"> bigger the influence of these parties will be in Europe.</span></div>
<blockquote>
<p><em>“This ugly rush to extremes is a vote of no confidence in the democratic system itself,”</em> Tisdall writes, noting that even in the <strong>US, once a "house of democracy," US President Donald Trump increasingly resembles a dictator rather than a democratic president.</strong></p>
</blockquote><div data-fuse="incontent_1"></div>
<h3 id="from-france-to-the-us-polarization-and-the-rise-of-populist-forces" class="ng-star-inserted"><span class="ng-star-inserted">From France to the US: Polarization and the rise of populist forces</span></h3>
<p>Across Europe, in the UK and the US, distrust and grievances deepen political dysfunction and social divisions daily.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><em>"Belief that democracy is the form of governance best suited to the modern world is dwindling, especially among younger people,” </em><strong>Tisdall</strong> notes.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Tisdall cites <strong>France</strong>, where <strong>permanent political crises</strong> are fueled by sharp polarization between left and right. But France is not alone: <strong>far-right and populist forces are gaining ground across Europe</strong>, from Britain to the Czech Republic, amid declining trust in moderate politicians.</p>
<p>Faith in democracy is also eroding outside wealthy Western nations. From <strong>Morocco to Bangladesh, Indonesia to Kenya</strong>, people are weary of <strong>poverty, corruption, and the lack of real alternatives</strong> to incumbent governments.</p><div data-fuse="incontent_2"></div>
<blockquote>
<p><em>“This is the fundamental challenge each faces: democracy isn’t working, or it is working so badly it risks being jettisoned,”</em> Tisdall writes.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>He argues that a <strong>global struggle is underway over whether democracy will survive as an ideology or the world will revert to an era of autocracies.</strong> So far, results vary: in <strong>Georgia</strong>, democracy has faltered; in <strong>Moldova</strong>, it has held.</p>
<h3 id="the-core-problem-when-democracy-stops-delivering-a-better-future" class="ng-star-inserted"><span class="ng-star-inserted">The core problem: When democracy stops delivering a better future</span></h3>
<p>According to Tisdall, the <strong>critical loss of faith in democratic systems</strong> stems from the fact that democracy <strong>no longer delivers consistent, tangible progress in quality of life</strong>, especially in the West. Instead of hope for a better future, people face <strong>inflation, job scarcity, rising wealth inequality, and mass migration</strong>.</p>
<p>All of this contributes to a <strong>deep and widespread sense of loss</strong> among people in democratic countries. Tisdall believes this explains the <strong>rise of populists</strong>, who promise to <strong>bring back the “good old days.”</strong></p>

          <div class="read-also">
          <div class="read-also__inner">
                          <h2 id="read-also" class="read-also__headline">
                Read also              </h2>
                        
            <ul class="read-also__list">
                        
                                  <li>
                                        
                                        
                      <a href="https://euromaidanpress.com/2019/08/16/putin-has-created-a-fifth-international-organizing-the-right-felshtinsky-says/" target="_blank" class="read-also__title">
                        <h3 id="putin-has-created-a-fifth-international-organizing-the-right-felshtinsky-says">Putin has created a Fifth International organizing the right, Felshtinsky says</h3>
                      </a>
                                      </li>
                  
                        
                                  <li>
                                        
                                        
                      <a href="https://euromaidanpress.com/2024/01/28/hungarian-parliamentary-party-lays-claim-to-ukraines-zakarpattia-region/" target="_blank" class="read-also__title">
                        <h3 id="hungary-far-right-party-calls-for-seizing-ukraines-zakarpattia-if-russia-wins">Hungary far-right party calls for seizing Ukraine’s Zakarpattia if Russia wins</h3>
                      </a>
                                      </li>
                  
                        
                                  <li>
                                        
                                        
                      <a href="https://euromaidanpress.com/2024/03/31/russia-suspected-of-funneling-funds-to-germanys-afd-party-for-pro-russian-messaging/" target="_blank" class="read-also__title">
                        <h3 id="russia-suspected-of-funneling-funds-to-germanys-afd-party-for-pro-russian-messaging">Russia suspected of funneling funds to Germany’s AfD party for pro-Russian messaging</h3>
                      </a>
                                      </li>
                  
                        
                  
                          </ul>
          </div>
      </div>
    


<p></p>

