		<item>
		<title>FT: American intelligence helped Ukraine attack over a dozen key Russian oil refineries since midsummer</title>
		<link>https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/10/12/ft-american-intelligence-helped-ukraine-attack-over-a-dozen-key-russian-oil-refineries-since-midsummer/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Yuri Zoria]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sun, 12 Oct 2025 11:56:57 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Latest news Ukraine]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Bashneft-UNPZ]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Belarus]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[China]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[deep strikes]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[drone strikes inside Russia]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Energy Aspects]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[fuel prices in Russia]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[fuel shortages]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[gasoline shortages]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[oil refineries]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Russian oil]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Russian oil refineries]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[US intelligence support]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://euromaidanpress.com/?p=366146</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[The support allegedly allowed Ukrainian drones to bypass Russian air defenses and damage more than 1mn barrels of daily refining capacity.]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><img width="1005" height="756" src="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/892da614-082c-4143-ac9e-411603ed1663.jpg" class="attachment-large size-large wp-post-image" alt="ft american intelligence helped ukraine attack over dozen key russian oil refineries since midsummer · post fire rises ilsky refinery following ukrainian drone strike 7 2025 telegram/supernova+ krasnodar krai news" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/892da614-082c-4143-ac9e-411603ed1663.jpg 1005w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/892da614-082c-4143-ac9e-411603ed1663-300x225.jpg 300w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/892da614-082c-4143-ac9e-411603ed1663-200x150.jpg 200w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/892da614-082c-4143-ac9e-411603ed1663-260x195.jpg 260w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/892da614-082c-4143-ac9e-411603ed1663-380x286.jpg 380w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/892da614-082c-4143-ac9e-411603ed1663-800x602.jpg 800w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1005px) 100vw, 1005px" /></p><div data-type="_mgwidget" data-widget-id="1845881"></div>        
        <script>
            (function(w,q){w[q]=w[q]||[];w[q].push(["_mgc.load"])})(window,"_mgq");
        </script>
    <p data-start="0" data-end="377">The Financial Times claims that US support has enabled Ukraine to strike deep into Russian territory, targeting vital oil refineries in a covert campaign that has severely disrupted Moscow’s fuel production. Since midsummer, American intelligence has reportedly played a significant role in helping Ukraine execute more than a dozen such attacks, escalating economic pressure on the Kremlin.</p>
<div class="pk-content-block pk-block-bg pk-block-bg-light" data-start="0" data-end="377">The FT report comes as Ukraine continues its campaign targeting Russian oil processing facilities. Since August, attacks on refineries have intensified, triggering gasoline shortages across multiple Russian regions. Repeated strikes are delaying repairs and preventing damaged facilities from quickly restoring production.</div>
<p data-start="447" data-end="1031">According to FT, multiple Ukrainian and US officials familiar with the campaign confirmed that Washington began sharing detailed intelligence with Kyiv earlier this year. The support intensified after a phone call in July between US President Donald Trump and Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy.</p><div data-fuse="incontent_1"></div>
<p data-start="447" data-end="1031">Following that conversation, four people briefed on the matter said the US began providing data with a new level of specificity — including flight path planning, altitude guidance, and vulnerability assessments — to improve the effectiveness of Ukraine’s long-range drone operations.</p>
<p data-start="1033" data-end="1454">Three sources told the FT that the US has been closely involved in the planning process. While a US official claimed that Ukraine independently selects its targets, other sources said Washington has also provided target priorities.</p>
<p data-start="1033" data-end="1454">One of them described Ukraine’s drone fleet as “the instrument” for a US effort to undermine Russia’s economic capacity and push President Vladimir Putin toward a negotiated settlement, pushed by Trump.</p>
<h3 id="16-oil-refineries-hit-as-russia-forced-to-import-fuel" data-start="1456" data-end="1513">16 oil refineries hit as Russia forced to import fuel</h3><div data-fuse="incontent_2"></div>
<p data-start="1515" data-end="2041">At least 16 out of Russia’s 38 oil refineries have been struck by Ukrainian forces — some of them repeatedly — significantly reducing Moscow’s refining output. According to Energy Aspects, a research group cited in the article, over 1mn barrels a day of refining capacity have been disrupted. The damage has driven up domestic fuel prices and led Russia to curtail diesel exports. Ukrainian President Zelenskyy stated that Moscow has turned to Belarus and China for petrol imports to compensate for its losses.</p>
<p data-start="2043" data-end="2473">Ukraine’s <a href="https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/10/11/ukraine-hits-key-military-fuel-supplier-1400-km-inside-russia-for-third-time-in-month/">recent strike on the Bashneft-UNPZ</a> refinery in Ufa — located about 1,400 kilometers from the Ukrainian border — marked the third such attack on energy facilities in Bashkortostan within a month.</p>
<p data-start="2475" data-end="2864">The Financial Times says that while Washington has publicly avoided acknowledging its direct role, the current level of coordination suggests a clear strategic shift in how the Trump administration is supporting Kyiv. A White House official stated the war “never would have happened” under Trump and that he is “trying to get it stopped”, but declined to comment on operational details.</p>
<p data-start="162" data-end="436"> </p>

          <div class="read-also">
          <div class="read-also__inner">
                          <h2 id="read-also" class="read-also__headline">
                Read also              </h2>
                        
            <ul class="read-also__list">
                        
                                  <li>
                                        
                                        
                      <a href="https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/10/11/ukraine-hits-key-military-fuel-supplier-1400-km-inside-russia-for-third-time-in-month/" target="_blank" class="read-also__title">
                        <h3 id="ukraine-hits-key-military-fuel-supplier-1400-km-inside-russia-for-third-time-in-month">Ukraine hits key military fuel supplier 1,400 km inside Russia for third time in month</h3>
                      </a>
                                      </li>
                  
                        
                                  <li>
                                        
                                        
                      <a href="https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/10/09/ukraine-hits-lukoil-gas-processing-plant-and-oil-facility-deep-inside-russia/" target="_blank" class="read-also__title">
                        <h3 id="ukraine-hits-lukoil-gas-processing-plant-and-oil-facility-deep-inside-russia">Ukraine hits Lukoil gas processing plant and oil facility deep inside Russia</h3>
                      </a>
                                      </li>
                  
                        
                                  <li>
                                        
                                        
                      <a href="https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/10/09/isw-putin-admits-ukraine-is-striking-refineries-but-claims-it-wont-help/" target="_blank" class="read-also__title">
                        <h3 id="isw-putin-admits-ukraine-is-striking-refineries-but-claims-it-wont-help">ISW: Putin admits Ukraine is striking refineries but claims it “won’t help”</h3>
                      </a>
                                      </li>
                  
                          </ul>
          </div>
      </div>
    
