		<enclosure url="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Do-you-understand-the-real-threat-from-Russia-1024x717.webp" length="46956" type="image/webp" />	</item>
		<item>
		<title>Ukrainian journalist Victoria Roshchyna posthumously named World Press Freedom Hero</title>
		<link>https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/10/11/ukrainian-journalist-victoria-roshchyna-posthumously-named-world-press-freedom-hero/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Maxim Volovich]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sat, 11 Oct 2025 16:38:13 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Latest news Ukraine]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Russian War Crimes]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[accountability]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[freedom of speech]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Human rights]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[International Media Support (IMS)]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[International Press Institute (IPI)]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[IPI World Congress 2025]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Journalism under fire]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Media freedom]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[press freedom]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Russian aggression]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Russian captivity]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Russian invasion of Ukraine]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Ukraine]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Ukrainian journalists]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Vienna 2025]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[war crimes]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[War crimes against journalists]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[World Press Freedom Hero award]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://euromaidanpress.com/?p=366053</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[Award honors journalist killed in Russian captivity for her fearless reporting from occupied Ukraine]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><img width="1024" height="635" src="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/world-press-freedom-hero-awards-2025-victoria-roshchyna-1024x635.jpg" class="attachment-large size-large wp-post-image" alt="Victoria Roshchyna among other 2025 IPI-IMS World Press Freedom Heroes honored by the International Press Institute and International Media Support" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/world-press-freedom-hero-awards-2025-victoria-roshchyna-1024x635.jpg 1024w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/world-press-freedom-hero-awards-2025-victoria-roshchyna-300x186.jpg 300w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/world-press-freedom-hero-awards-2025-victoria-roshchyna-1536x952.jpg 1536w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/world-press-freedom-hero-awards-2025-victoria-roshchyna-380x236.jpg 380w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/world-press-freedom-hero-awards-2025-victoria-roshchyna-800x496.jpg 800w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/world-press-freedom-hero-awards-2025-victoria-roshchyna-1160x719.jpg 1160w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/world-press-freedom-hero-awards-2025-victoria-roshchyna.jpg 1925w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></p><div data-type="_mgwidget" data-widget-id="1845881"></div>        
        <script>
            (function(w,q){w[q]=w[q]||[];w[q].push(["_mgc.load"])})(window,"_mgq");
        </script>
    
<p>Victoria Roshchyna, a Ukrainian journalist who died in Russian captivity, has been posthumously <a href="https://ipi.media/2025-world-press-freedom-hero-award/">named</a> a 2025 IPI-IMS World Press Freedom Hero. The award will be presented on 24 October 2025 at the University of Vienna during the IPI World Congress and Media Innovation Festival.</p>



<p>The honor recognizes her exceptional courage and resilience in documenting life under Russian occupation and the human cost of war. Her death on 19 September 2024 underscores the extreme dangers faced by journalists reporting from conflict zones and the urgent need to hold perpetrators of press repression accountable.</p>



<h3 id="captured-twice-for-reporting-the-truth" class="wp-block-heading"><a></a>Captured twice for reporting the truth</h3>



<div class="wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow" style="flex-basis:33.33%">
<figure class="wp-block-gallery-3 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex">
<figure><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="1024" data-id="366085" src="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/victoria-roshchyna-ukrainian-journalist-portrait-3-1024x1024.jpeg" alt="" class="wp-image-366085" srcset="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/victoria-roshchyna-ukrainian-journalist-portrait-3-1024x1024.jpeg 1024w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/victoria-roshchyna-ukrainian-journalist-portrait-3-300x300.jpeg 300w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/victoria-roshchyna-ukrainian-journalist-portrait-3-80x80.jpeg 80w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/victoria-roshchyna-ukrainian-journalist-portrait-3-110x110.jpeg 110w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/victoria-roshchyna-ukrainian-journalist-portrait-3-380x380.jpeg 380w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/victoria-roshchyna-ukrainian-journalist-portrait-3-800x799.jpeg 800w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/victoria-roshchyna-ukrainian-journalist-portrait-3-1160x1159.jpeg 1160w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/victoria-roshchyna-ukrainian-journalist-portrait-3-45x45.jpeg 45w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/victoria-roshchyna-ukrainian-journalist-portrait-3.jpeg 1280w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /><figcaption>Ukrainian journalist Victoria Roshchyna. Source: X</figcaption></figure>
</figure>
</div>



<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow" style="flex-basis:66.66%">
<p>Victoria Roshchyna was a freelance Ukrainian journalist known for her fearless coverage from frontlines and occupied territories. She filmed videos and wrote articles from hotspots in eastern and southern Ukraine, including temporarily occupied Enerhodar, and prepared reports on fighting in Zaporizhzhia and Donetsk oblasts. She had also planned to travel to Mariupol while it was under Russian siege in 2022.</p>
</div>
</div>



<p>Roshchyna was first detained by Russian forces in March 2022 in temporarily occupied Berdiansk. She was held for 10 days and later released. Refusing to be silenced, she continued reporting.</p><div data-fuse="incontent_1"></div>



<p>In August 2023, she disappeared during another trip to Russian-occupied territories. She had left Ukraine for Poland on 27 July 2023, intending to reach occupied areas via Russia, and lost contact after 3 August.</p>



<p>Her body was returned to Ukraine during a prisoner exchange on 14 February 2025, mislabeled as an “unidentified male.” Forensic experts later identified it as Roshchyna’s, with a DNA test confirming a 99% match.</p>



<pre class="wp-block-preformatted">Signs of torture and severe injuries were found on her body. Internal organs — including the brain, eyeballs, and part of the trachea — were missing, raising suspicions of an attempted cover-up.</pre>



<p>A forensic exam conducted by the Main Bureau of Forensic Medical Examination of the Ministry of Health of Ukraine on 9 July 2025 confirmed a neck injury, bone fractures, hemorrhages in the soft tissues of the temporal region, right shoulder, and lower legs, and abrasions of the left foot. All these traumas obviously couldn't have been self-inflicted.</p>



<h3 id="a-symbol-of-courage-and-sacrifice" class="wp-block-heading"><a></a>A symbol of courage and sacrifice</h3>



<p>The International Press Institute (IPI) and International Media Support (IMS) recognized Roshchyna for her immense personal sacrifice in pursuit of truth. Her story revealed the brutal treatment endured by Ukrainian journalists in Russian captivity.</p><div data-fuse="incontent_2"></div>



<pre class="wp-block-preformatted">Anna Babinets, editor of Slidstvo.Info, described her as a “very talented and brave journalist” who believed in exposing the stories of civilians murdered and tortured in Russian-occupied areas.</pre>



<h3 id="honoring-global-defenders-of-press-freedom" class="wp-block-heading"><a></a>Honoring global defenders of press freedom</h3>



<p>The IPI-IMS World Press Freedom Hero award is given annually to journalists who show extraordinary commitment to free expression. The 2025 edition, marking IPI’s 75th anniversary, honors seven journalists worldwide—including Roshchyna and Mariam Abu Dagga, both killed while reporting from war zones.</p>



<p>Two other recipients remain imprisoned. The awards highlight a growing global crisis as authoritarian regimes suppress independent journalism with impunity.</p>



<h3 id="a-call-to-defend-media-freedom" class="wp-block-heading"><a></a>A call to defend media freedom</h3>



<p>Roshchyna’s posthumous recognition serves as a stark reminder that truth-telling can be deadly under tyranny. It renews the call to protect journalists working in war zones and to ensure accountability for crimes against the press.</p><div data-fuse="incontent_3"></div>



<p>Her legacy symbolizes the resilience of Ukrainian journalism amid Russia’s attempts to silence it.</p>



<h3 id="roshchynas-background" class="wp-block-heading"><a></a>Roshchyna’s background</h3>



<p>Before her capture, Victoria Roshchyna worked for <em>Hromadske</em> and contributed to <em>Ukrainska Pravda</em> and <em>Radio Svoboda</em>. In 2022, she <a href="https://www.frontlinedefenders.org/en/profile/victoria-roshchyna?utm_source=chatgpt.com">received</a> the International Women’s Media Foundation’s “For Courage in Journalism” award. On 4 September 2025, she was posthumously <a href="https://mezha.net/eng/bukvy/ukrainian-journalist-viktoria-roshchyna-receives-posthumous-oxi-courage-award/">honored</a> with the Oxi Courage Award.</p>



<p>She was also posthumously awarded Ukraine’s Order of Freedom by President Volodymyr Zelenskyy and the Oxi Courage Award in Washington.</p>



<h3 id="related" class="wp-block-heading"><a></a>Related:</h3>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><a href="https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/08/02/tortured-ukrainian-reporter-victoria-roshchyna-honored-with-highest-state-award-after-death-in-russian-captivity/">Tortured Ukrainian reporter Victoria Roshchyna honored with highest state award after death in Russian captivity</a></li>



<li><a href="https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/08/08/kyiv-buried-journalist-victoria-roshchyna-murdered-in-russian-captivity/">Kyiv buried journalist Victoria Roshchyna, murdered in Russian captivity</a></li>
</ul>



<p></p>



<p></p>

